. /*      
> We construct the outcome variable, leftist_std, by standardizing responses (m
> ean = 0, standard deviation = 1) to survey question "plh0004", which asks res
> pondents about their political leaning in a scale from 0 to 10. We also flip 
> the sign so that a higher number represents a political preference towards th
> e left.
> 
> We estimate a linear regression model where the primary independent variable 
> is an indicator for whether the respondent has a daughter. The specification 
> controls for a rich set of covariates: respondent's gender, age, income, year
> s of education, nationality, marital status, survey year, and the age of the 
> child. The coefficient on the daughter variable is interpreted as the margina
> l effect of having a daughter (versus a son) on left political leaning, expre
> ssed in standard deviation units.
> 
> The sample is restricted to individuals with exactly one child. We also keep 
> only one observation per person by keeping the first valid observation for ea
> ch individual. To minimize child's gender selection, we exclude homosexuals.
> */      
